## Project-Specific SOP Considerations
- **meta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel** — no stdout JSON parsing, no fallback recovery. All SOP and agent contracts must enforce this strictly.
- **No pre-invocation sidecar writes** — the runner does not touch markdown files before coder invocation.
- **No markdown write-backs** — no `sync_review_metadata`, `stamp_created_metadata`, etc.
- **Explicit exception routing** — hard failures go to `route_after_failure()` immediately.
- **Authority precedence**: Runner logic > SOP + Status Rules > Artifact metadata > Artifact body.
- **Backward compatibility**: Existing `agent-runner run` execution path must remain unchanged; daemon features are additive.
- **Conservative recovery**: v1 daemon uses manual recovery after worker crash — no automatic resume of partial coder steps.
- **Database transactions**: All state-changing operations wrapped in transactions; claiming uses SKIP LOCKED to avoid blocking.
- **Testing**: No LLM calls in tests — use mocked providers or fixture-based workflows.
- **Active initiative**: Daemon mode with PostgreSQL-backed job management (PLAN-20260602-01) is in progress — 12 tasks across 4 phases.

